[2026-05-11T07:32:01.889Z] [INFO] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_464","type":"reasoning","text":"**Considering PR body updates**\n\nI'm noticing the git status returned no status line, which is curious, but it still shows the current branch and log, so that's good. I think I need to update the PR body to include the Deno test command since we ran it and fixed the CI. It makes sense to mention the CI success too. To edit the PR body, I can use `gh pr edit` with a heredoc. I just need to confirm that approach is suitable.\n**Editing PR description**\n\nI'm considering how to update the PR description to include the Deno test and CI run. Even though I could skip mentioning Deno, the local verification list feels incomplete after the last commit since we did run `deno test --allow-read` and another test command. It seems necessary to add those details and possibly note the CI success too. I could use `gh pr edit 27 --body-file -` for this, using a here-doc. That approach should work fine."}}
